{#- MOVILIDAD POST-ENTRENO — the after-session sibling of the activation matrix.
    Home doc: `mobility-brief.md`. Built September 3, 2026 from Iván's
    "Sistema Maestro de Movilidad" source doc, section A of each sport.

    Two questions -> one of 15 routines (sport x duration). Same engine, same
    setup pattern and the same CSS file as /members/activacion/.

    *** THE FIVE DECISIONS TAKEN BEFORE BUILDING, all Iván's, all reversals of
    the source doc. Read these before editing anything:

    1. DURATIONS ARE 10/20/30, NOT the source's 30/45/60. Nobody does an hour of
       stretching after a session; 30 minutes is longer than several sessions in
       his own plans. The 30/45/60 ladder is not wrong, it is the RECOVERY-DAY
       ladder, and it goes on that tool (section B of the source doc), which is
       a separate artifact by Iván's call. Do not "restore" the source numbers
       here.

    2. THE BASE ROUTINES ARE MAT-ONLY (plus a wall, which the copy declares).
       The source opened three of five sports on a foam roller and also needed a
       lacrosse ball, a doorframe, a yoga block and a chair - while the promise
       was "you only need a mat". Roller and ball work is preserved as
       `variants`, which the engine already swaps in and whose button hides
       itself when a routine has none. No third axis, promise stays true.

    3. INTENSITY, NOT DEPTH, is what separates this tool from the recovery-day
       one. Post-session is 45-60s holds at submaximal range on tissue that was
       just loaded. The source's 60-minute tiers put passive frog and winged
       dragon (Yin) on freshly damaged tissue; that work belongs on a fresh day.
       So the third tier here adds COVERAGE and a real downshift, not range.

    4. TRIATHLON IS THE BRICK and "todo el cuerpo" is sport-neutral. Otherwise
       the two produce near-identical lists and one of them should not exist.
       `tri` = quads and calves from the run + hip flexors from the bike + lats
       from the swim. `all` = no sport assumed, and it also serves a gym day.

    5. "Agnostic" became "Todo el cuerpo". The word means nothing to an athlete.

    *** CLINICAL: three things from the source are deliberately absent. All three
    are reversals of a prescription that looks completely normal on the page.

    - THE SLEEPER STRETCH (source 3.A #4, swimmers). Already rejected twice in
      this repo in writing - `swimmer-shoulder-brief.md` §3 calls it "the
      impingement position, loaded" and says do not re-add it, and the
      activation matrix cites it as the reference class for the dislocates
      decision. Replaced by `crossBody`, the cross-body horizontal adduction
      stretch, which reaches the same posterior capsule without compressing the
      joint. Its cue carries the part that makes it work: depress the scapula
      and do not let the shoulder travel forward.
    - THE DOORFRAME PEC STRETCH (source 3.A #2 and 4.A #5). End-range
      glenohumeral extension on a fatigued cuff, in the population whose
      anterior capsule is typically lax rather than stiff - same family of error
      as the sleeper. Replaced by `pecFloorProne`, which is floor-based and
      self-limiting, and whose cue caps it at the chest rather than the joint.
    - USTRASANA / CAMEL (source 2.A 45min). Loaded end-range lumbar extension
      with the neck back on a fatigued athlete post-ride. It is the one item
      here where a real injury is plausible, and the same routine already gets
      thoracic extension and hip flexor length three other ways.

    Also reworded rather than removed: the source's "foam roller enfocado
    AGRESIVAMENTE en banda IT". The IT band is not contractile and does not
    lengthen; the targets are TFL and vastus lateralis, and "aggressively"
    contradicts the source's own never-past-7/10 instruction. `itCross` carries
    the correct target and says so in the cue.

    *** BOX BREATHING IS NOT REBUILT HERE. The source's 60-minute tiers spend
    5-8 minutes on it and on savasana. /members/respiracion/ already owns box
    breathing, so `breathFloor` does the closing downshift with a simple 4-6
    pattern and LINKS OUT. Same one-home argument that put swimming inside the
    activation tool rather than on its own page.

    *** EVERY NOTE ABOUT THIS PAGE BELONGS IN THIS BLOCK. Almost the whole page
    is inside {% raw %}, where a Nunjucks comment is NOT a comment - it is
    literal text that renders to the reader. That happened on the activation
    page on Sept 3, 2026 and Iván saw it live. `automation/build-sanity.js` now
    fails the build on any surviving template delimiter, but the simpler rule is
    to write the note here or use an HTML comment.

    Two notes that would otherwise be inline:

    - The sport question uses `.setup-opts--wrap`, added to
      members-activacion.css for this page. Five children at `flex: 1` are 65px
      wide at 390px and every label wraps to three lines.
    - The pain aside is sport-aware and always visible for at least one tool,
      because every sport here has somewhere to hand off to. That is
      methodology.md §11 respected in the product: this is mobility, not rehab. -#}
